{# The ONE place a social provider button is drawn - /login, /register and the
   "Connected sign-in methods" card all include it, so they cannot drift.
   Each button follows its provider's brand rules, not the site's styles
   (assets/styles/components/_social-signin.scss explains each one). Logos are
   inlined (_social_provider_logo.html.twig, shared with the
   connected-provider badges in settings), so no external image ever loads.

   Wording is "Continue with {provider}" everywhere, the connect buttons in
   settings too: Apple allows only Sign in / Sign up / Continue with Apple,
   Google and Meta list "Continue with" among theirs.

   Parameters: provider ('google'|'apple'|'facebook'), href, size ('sm' or empty),
   full_width (bool). #}
{% set provider_name = {google: 'Google', apple: 'Apple', facebook: 'Facebook'}[provider] %}
<a class="btn btn-{{ provider }}-signin{{ size|default('') == 'sm' ? ' btn-sm' : '' }}{{ full_width|default(false) ? ' w-100' : '' }}" href="{{ href }}" data-turbo="false">
    {{- include('_social_provider_logo.html.twig', {provider: provider, class: 'btn-' ~ provider ~ '-signin-logo'}) -}}
    {{ 'auth.social.continue_with'|trans({'%provider%': provider_name}) }}
</a>
